WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.551
Inferences

00:00:01.931 --> 00:00:04.257
Pick what MUST be true, not what COULD be.

00:00:05.457 --> 00:00:06.547
How to spot it

00:00:06.947 --> 00:00:08.950
A passage that ends in a blank

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.262
The question says “most logically completes the text”

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:17.765
It’s testing: logic: what the evidence actually proves

00:00:18.965 --> 00:00:19.731
The method

00:00:20.131 --> 00:00:23.128
Step 1: Paraphrase each sentence

00:00:23.408 --> 00:00:24.756
A few words each.

00:00:25.306 --> 00:00:27.672
Step 2: Find the key evidence

00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:30.385
A surprise, or two facts to combine.

00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:33.656
Step 3: Predict the conclusion

00:00:33.936 --> 00:00:35.124
If A and B, then…

00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:37.573
Step 4: Cut “could be true”

00:00:37.853 --> 00:00:39.432
And anything too strong.

00:00:39.982 --> 00:00:41.076
In a few words

00:00:41.226 --> 00:00:44.508
Evidence. Predict. Must be true.

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:46.775
Logic rules

00:00:47.175 --> 00:00:49.180
Must be true beats could be true

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:50.949
Combine the facts

00:00:51.229 --> 00:00:53.452
The answer usually links two of them.

00:00:54.002 --> 00:00:55.504
Watch the small words

00:00:55.784 --> 00:00:57.666
only, unlike, before, most

00:00:58.216 --> 00:00:59.726
Modest beats extreme

00:01:00.006 --> 00:01:02.595
“May have contributed” beats “caused all”.

00:01:03.795 --> 00:01:04.856
Let’s try one

00:01:05.256 --> 00:01:11.431
Archaeologists excavating a 9,000-year-old village found seeds of wild barley in the oldest layers

00:01:11.431 --> 00:01:18.007
of soil. In layers dating to about 500 years later, they found barley seeds with tough stems that

00:01:18.007 --> 00:01:24.175
do not shatter and scatter seeds on their own, a trait that appears only when people repeatedly harvest

00:01:24.175 --> 00:01:28.038
and replant a crop. These findings suggest that ______

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.582
Which choice most logically completes the text?

00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:35.739
Fact one: the oldest layers have wild barley.

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:41.654
Fact two: later layers show a trait that appears only when people farm barley.

00:01:42.204 --> 00:01:48.749
Combine them: farming started in between. Nothing in the text proves A, B, or D. Choice C.

00:01:49.949 --> 00:01:51.018
Common traps

00:01:51.418 --> 00:01:52.350
Could be true

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.102
Sounds smart. Never proven.

00:01:55.652 --> 00:01:56.501
Reversal

00:01:56.781 --> 00:01:58.590
Gets the direction backwards.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:00.741
Inferences

00:02:01.021 --> 00:02:04.302
Evidence. Predict. Must be true.

00:02:04.852 --> 00:02:05.432
Spot it

00:02:05.632 --> 00:02:09.291
Passage ends in a blank: “most logically completes”

00:02:09.841 --> 00:02:10.548
Steps

00:02:10.748 --> 00:02:12.719
1. Paraphrase each sentence

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.715
2. Find the key evidence

00:02:14.995 --> 00:02:16.849
3. Predict the conclusion

00:02:17.129 --> 00:02:19.464
4. Cut could-be-true and too-strong

00:02:20.014 --> 00:02:20.738
Remember

00:02:20.938 --> 00:02:22.943
Must be true beats could be true

00:02:23.223 --> 00:02:24.557
Combine two facts

00:02:24.837 --> 00:02:27.029
Watch: only, unlike, before, most

00:02:27.309 --> 00:02:28.819
Modest beats extreme

00:02:29.369 --> 00:02:29.810
Trap

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.887
Sounds smart, never proven

